2. AI-generated raster assets
-----------------------------

The 32 PNG images under frontend/assets/, frontend/public/,
frontend/src/assets/ and backend/app/static/ were generated with OpenAI's
image API. Each file carries a C2PA Content Credentials manifest recording
that provenance, which anyone can verify; the manifests are left intact rather
than stripped.

Ownership of the generated images rests with the PlateMate authors under
OpenAI's terms of use, so they are covered by LICENSE.


3. 3D character model and animations
------------------------------------

The remaining 24 files under frontend/public/biped/ — the character mesh and
its animations — were produced by the PlateMate authors and exported from
Blender. They carry no third-party author or license metadata and are covered
by LICENSE.


4. Dependency licenses
----------------------

Dependencies are not vendored here; they are installed from npm and PyPI and
keep their own licenses.

All 34 direct frontend dependencies are MIT or Apache-2.0. Across the 306
packages that resolve transitively, the licenses are MIT, ISC, Apache-2.0,
BSD-2/3-Clause, 0BSD, BlueOak-1.0.0, Unlicense, and CC-BY-4.0 for caniuse-lite,
which ships browser-support data rather than code. All are permissive.

psycopg2-binary is distributed under the LGPL with exceptions. It is used as
an unmodified library, which the LGPL permits from a project under a different
license; modifying psycopg2 itself would carry the LGPL's own obligations.

Three unused frontend dependencies were removed rather than carried into a
public release: gsap (not an OSI-approved license), components@0.1.0 (no
license declared, upstream abandoned) and npm (added by mistake).
